  <revision rev="2" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>48a28d59b0eefcd6d4ebe05b74ab189c</srcmd5>
    <version>0.11.46</version>
    <time>1787656858</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update to 0.11.46 and relax the bundle dependencies from exact '=' pins to
'&gt;=' floors.

0.11.46 changes nothing but the pinned bundle versions: -core 0.3.320,
-json 0.1.55, -media-assets-01 0.1.33. Module code, README and LICENSE are
byte-identical to 0.11.44.

PLEASE STAGE TOGETHER with the rest of this release train, which is
submitted as separate requests:
  sr#1373544  python-comfyui-workflow-templates-json          0.1.55
  sr#1373547  python-comfyui-workflow-templates-media-assets-01 0.1.33
  sr#1373548  python-comfyui-workflow-templates-core           0.3.320
The four packages are only consistent as a set: -core's manifest names the
assets that live in -json and -media-assets-01.

On the pin change: upstream's '==' is a release-train lockfile, not an API
constraint. This meta package's only code imports five stable helpers from
-core, and the bundles are additive asset stores, so the real requirement is
one-directional -- a bundle OLDER than the manifest -core ships means a
missing asset. A floor states exactly that; '=' additionally forbids the
harmless newer direction, and that is not theoretical: while preparing this
train, bumping -core alone immediately made the 0.11.44 meta package
unresolvable in the devel project.

Verified in the build chroot with the built RPMs installed: all 528
templates and all 1235 assets resolve via iter_assets(), including the six
new ones (api_wan3_0_{t2v,i2v,r2v}, api_meshy7_{text,image}_to_model,
api_bytedance_vcube_video_enhance).
</comment>
    <requestid>1373549</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="3" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>904dfadc47381c0f9ea9b68a724b4ceb</srcmd5>
    <version>0.11.48</version>
    <time>1787766812</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update python-comfyui-workflow-templates to 0.11.48.

Upstream moves only the pinned bundle versions in this release: -core to
0.3.322, -json to 0.1.57 and -media-assets-01 to 0.1.35. The module code,
README and license are byte-identical to 0.11.46. Those three bundles are
submitted alongside this request.

The spec's bundle dependency floors are raised to match what 0.11.48 pins.
Upstream uses &quot;==&quot; for these; the spec keeps them as &quot;&gt;=&quot; floors for the
reason recorded in the comment above the Requires block -- the constraint is
one-directional, and an exact pin makes the package uninstallable on every
independent bundle release. The four bundles upstream did not move
(media-api 0.3.84, media-video 0.3.101, media-image 0.3.160,
media-other 0.3.229) keep their existing floors.

Staging: these four requests must land in the SAME staging project. Factory
currently has -core 0.3.320, -json 0.1.55 and -media-assets-01 0.1.33; this
package's raised BuildRequires and Requires need 0.3.322 / 0.1.57 / 0.1.35, so
splitting the batch across stagings leaves this package unresolvable.

Sequencing: please stage this together with, or after, SR 1373695, which
converts comfyui's exact &quot;=&quot; pins on this package family to floors. Until
1373695 is accepted, Factory's comfyui still requires
python3XX-comfyui-workflow-templates = 0.11.44, so a staging that takes this
bump without 1373695 will show comfyui broken in installcheck. 0.11.48
satisfies the &quot;&gt;= 0.11.44&quot; floor 1373695 introduces, so no comfyui spec
change is needed.</comment>
    <requestid>1373740</requestid>
  </revision>
